    {
      "id": "e034d0179aa9",
      "name": "l1-hindsight-promote",
      "prompt": "Read ~/.hermes/memory-facts/staging.md. For each bullet line in that file:\n\n1. Strip the timestamp and score prefix (e.g. \"- [2026-07-09T09:27Z] [score=3] \").\n\n2. Parse ALL inline tags from the line before extracting fact text:\n   - Memory type: [type=fact], [type=correction], [type=outcome], [type=preference], [type=reasoning], [type=observation]. Default: \"fact\".\n   - Volatility class: [vc=stable], [vc=volatile], [vc=ephemeral]. Default: \"volatile\".\n   - Memory namespace: [ns=profile], [ns=event], [ns=record]. Default: \"record\".\n   - Anchors: [anchors: term1, term2, term3] — split on comma.\n   - Entities: [entities: Type:Name, Type:Name] — split on comma.\n   - Valid-from: [valid_from=<ISO timestamp>] — use as the temporal anchor.\n   - Retention score: [retention=<float>] — include as a tag.\n   - Supersedes: [supersedes=<id>] — include as a tag.\n   - Access count: [access_count=<int>] — pass through.\n   Strip ALL of these tag patterns from the line before extracting the clean fact text.\n\n3. Build the hindsight_retain call:\n   - content = clean fact text (all tags removed)\n   - context = \"l1-extract\"\n   - tags = [\n       \"l1\",\n       \"type:<memory_type>\",\n       \"volatility:<volatility_class>\",\n       \"ns:<memory_namespace>\",\n     ]\n     + [\"entity:<entity_str>\" for each entity in entities list]\n     + [\"anchor:<anchor>\" for each anchor in anchors list]\n     + ([\"valid_from:<valid_from>\"] if valid_from)\n     + ([\"retention:<retention>\"] if retention present)\n     + ([\"supersedes:<supersedes_id>\"] if supersedes present)\n\n4. For types \"correction\" and \"outcome\": bypass the recurrence check — retain immediately (high-signal one-time events).\n\n5. BEFORE running l1-graphiti-write.py and BEFORE truncating staging.md:\n   Register all facts as pending in graphiti-state.db so we have a durable record:\n   run: python3 ~/.hermes/scripts/l1-graphiti-reconcile.py register\n   This ensures facts are recoverable even if Graphiti write fails.\n\n6. After retaining all facts via hindsight_retain, run this shell command to also write them to the Graphiti knowledge graph:\n   python3 ~/.hermes/scripts/l1-graphiti-write.py ~/.hermes/memory-facts/staging.md 2>&1\n   IMPORTANT: capture the output and exit code. Run it BEFORE truncating staging.md.\n   - If it succeeds: mark facts written with:\n     echo \"<script output>\" | python3 ~/.hermes/scripts/l1-graphiti-reconcile.py mark-written\n   - If it fails (non-zero exit or error lines in output): log the failure.\n     Do NOT abort the job — the reconcile cron will retry. Proceed to truncate.\n\n7. After retaining all facts and running l1-graphiti-write.py, REPLACE the contents of staging.md with an empty string (truncate it): write an empty string to ~/.hermes/memory-facts/staging.md\n\n8. Finally run: python3 ~/.hermes/scripts/l1-graphiti-reconcile.py status\n   to confirm the DB state. Report the summary.",
