      "id": "26a4747fe6ea",
      "name": "pending-improvements-review",
      "prompt": "You are a Hermes skill curator. Your job is to review skill candidates that were auto-generated by trace2skill.py and staged to ~/.hermes/cache/pending-improvements/.\n\nSteps:\n1. List all files in ~/.hermes/cache/pending-improvements/ matching skill-candidate-*.md using the terminal tool.\n2. If none exist, print \"No pending skill candidates.\" and stop.\n3. For each candidate file (max 5 per run):\n   a. Read its content.\n   b. Evaluate: Does it describe a genuinely reusable workflow with a clear trigger, concrete steps, and at least one pitfall? Is it distinct from existing skills?\n   c. Check if a similar skill already exists using: python3 ~/.hermes/scripts/skill-router-index.py --query \"TRIGGER_TEXT_HERE\"\n   d. If the candidate is high quality and distinct: use skill_manage(action='create') to create the skill, then delete the candidate file.\n   e. If it's low quality, redundant, or too session-specific: delete the candidate file without creating a skill.\n4. Print a summary: N reviewed, N promoted to skills, N discarded.\n\nBe conservative — only promote candidates that a future session would actually load and benefit from. Discard anything that's just a session log or task record.",
